WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.050
Our class is choosing a

2
00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.210
snack for Sports Day.

3
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.610
Everyone shouted at once!

4
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.850
How can we find out what most of you want?

5
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.570
Today: ask a question, collect

6
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.190
the answers, and count them.

7
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.380
Data is facts we collect to

8
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.140
answer a question.

9
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.830
Our question: which snack

10
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.910
do you like best?

11
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.800
Each answer is one piece of data.

12
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.720
To count fast, use tally marks.

13
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.730
Draw one line for each answer.

14
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.840
Four lines, then the fifth

15
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:35.760
goes across them.

16
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.890
Then count in fives: five, ten, fifteen!

17
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.480
Here are our answers.

18
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.700
Oranges: twelve.

19
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.780
Bananas: seven.

20
00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.770
Mangoes: nine.

21
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.480
Oranges win!

22
00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:52.170
Quick check!

23
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.170
How do you write seven with tally marks?

24
00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.770
One group of five, with the fifth

25
00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.210
line across, and two more lines.

26
00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.550
Groups of five make counting

27
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:05.570
quick, and hard to get wrong.

28
00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.190
Computers count exactly what is written.

29
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.720
If one list says Musa and another

30
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.200
says Moussa, the computer thinks

31
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.360
there are two pupils!

32
00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.100
In the app, two teachers wrote the

33
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.060
same class list in different ways.

34
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.640
Tap “Match the class list”.

35
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.020
Watch the computer's count go from

36
00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.340
twenty names to eight pupils!

37
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:31.300
Your turn.

38
00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:36.550
A list says Musa, Moussa and Musah.

39
00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.550
How many pupils can a computer see?

40
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.700
Three: to a computer, every way of

41
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.080
writing is a different name.

42
00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.250
Remember: data is facts we

43
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.090
collect to answer a question.

44
00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.320
Tally marks count fast, in fives.

45
00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.570
And always count carefully.

46
00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.600
Try it tomorrow: ask ten people at

47
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.620
home or at school one question.

48
00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.130
What's your favourite fruit, maybe?

49
00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.630
Keep a tally, then count.

50
00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.590
Which answer won?
